        <info>The buyer's letter of intent has arrived, normally through the appointed broker. Log it against this disposition and record the price and key terms exactly as offered - this is the buyer's position, not ours.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Received</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The terms are being reviewed internally. Work through price, due diligence period, closing period and earnest money against what the disposition needs, and decide whether to counter or to execute as offered.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Under Review</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The negotiation is underway. Record every round - ours and the buyer's - by logging it in the Counter History on this record; the named counter-round buttons are retired, so every exchange is logged the same way regardless of who sent it. Stay on this step for as long as the negotiation runs. Advance only once both sides are agreed.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Negotiation</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>Both sides are agreed and the LOI is signed. Attach the executed document, then move the disposition on with Advance to PSA - on a sale our own legal team prepares the contract and issues the first draft.</info>
